<BaseLayout title="Contribute and review" description="Submit a versioned technical review of the O2AT v0.2 proposal using section references, evidence and compatibility analysis.">
  <div class="wrap page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Review the proposal</p><h1>Specific questions make useful review.</h1><p class="lead">O2AT is an engineering draft. Reviews are most useful when they identify a section, provide evidence and explain the compatibility effect of a proposed change.</p></div>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Review scope</p><h2>Start with the wire behaviour.</h2></div><div class="prose"><ul><li>Can two independent teams implement the fixed header, descriptors, state transitions and counter semantics without interpreting unstated defaults?</li><li>Are MTU, VLAN, padding, FCS and occupied-time calculations correct for the stated MAC service?</li><li>Do credit updates account for sent-but-not-yet-consumed data and keep packet events causal under delay?</li><li>Are source pacing, common-frequency operation and fixed-rate live input distinguished accurately?</li><li>Can the reference-loss and holdover policy be tested without relying on remote STATUS delivery for local protection?</li><li>Does a proposed change affect header interpretation, capability negotiation, packet sizing, clock state or interoperability?</li></ul></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section-top"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Contribution route</p><h2>Use the public issue tracker.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Use the project’s public GitHub issue tracker for technical review and reproducible defects. Do not include private equipment, infrastructure details, access tokens or unpublished customer information.</p><p class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/o2at-org/o2at/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open a review issue</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/o2at-org/o2at" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the project repository</a></p><p>Implementation notes, bench records and compatibility tables live in the <a href="https://wiki.o2at.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">O2AT engineering wiki</a>. Reading is open to everyone; to comment there, request a reviewer account through a <a href="https://github.com/o2at-org/o2at/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub issue</a>. Long-form updates are published on <a href="https://linuxprophet.substack.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Substack</a>.</p><p>Submission does not imply adoption. A protocol change is accepted only in a numbered revision with an explicit compatibility note and updated test vectors. Review comments remain distinguishable from adopted requirements.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section-top"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Governance and licences</p><h2>Open review is not certification.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>The v0.2 paper proposes open software/RTL and hardware licensing directions. The website code, specification prose, any future RTL or hardware files, third-party standards, trademarks and vendor materials are distinct works. A proposed licence does not establish patent clearance or grant rights over third-party material.</p><p>Published by the Open Optical Audio Transport Project. Originator and specification editor credits are recorded in <a href="https://github.com/o2at-org/o2at/blob/main/CONTRIBUTORS.md">CONTRIBUTORS.md</a>. The paper is currently a proposal for review. No manufacturer endorsement, independent peer review or standards approval is represented here.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
